==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|interrogatus}}, past participle of {{m|la|interrogare||to ask, question}}, from {{m|la|inter||between}} + {{m|la|rogare||to ask}}; see [[rogation]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-interrogate.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|interrogat}}

# {{label|en|transitive}} To [[question]] or [[quiz]], especially in a [[thorough]] and/or [[aggressive]] manner.
#: ''The police '''interrogated''' the suspect at some length before they let him go.''

